;tree utils
;So the basic Z-machine object relationship model is that everything has a parent (can be zero), 
;could have a sibling (if that is non-zero) and could have a child (if that's non-zero)

;An object with no children given a child has to update its child number
;and the child updates the parent number but has no siblings yet

;adding a second object means the new one also updates its parent, then there's a tree walk 
;down to the child and across siblings until a zero is found then the zero is replaced by 
;the object number of the new child (sibling to end child) 
;and the new child gets the new parent.

;
;param 1: object being moved
;param 2: destination object
routine move_object()
byte 04
word 0,0,0,0
    get_child l02 -> l03 .children
    ;destination has no children
    remove_obj l01 ; disconnect from current location
    insert_obj l01 l02 ; add it to destination
.children ; target object has children
    get_sibling l03 -> l04 [false].add
    ;insert object into new sibling chain
.lp
    lp

    rtrue

 